2. DATA WE PROCESS

Account and authentication: name, email address, optional profile picture,
account identifiers, sign-in provider details, verification/reset tokens,
and session information. You can register with email and password or sign
in with Google, GitHub, or LinkedIn. Email/password accounts store a
password hash, not the plaintext password. We do not receive your sign-in
provider's password. Session records can include IP address and user agent.

Your activity: watchlists, saved jobs and companies, search/filter criteria,
alert and language preferences, application status, notes, interview or
other tracking details you choose to enter, and associated timestamps.

Search and Narrowed: natural-language search text and language, saved
Narrowed criteria, matching decisions, feedback, and usage records needed
to deliver and troubleshoot the feature. Free text may contain personal
data you include. Please keep it about the work you are seeking and avoid
sensitive personal information or confidential information about others.

Billing, when you purchase Pro: email, internal account reference, Paddle
customer/subscription identifiers, subscription status, billing dates, and
trial usage. Paddle collects payment and billing details through its own
checkout. We do not store full payment-card details.

Technical and support information: network and device information needed
to serve and secure requests, rate-limit and diagnostic records, aggregate
usage/performance measurements, and messages you send to support.

Public job content may contain recruiters' names or business contact
information. It comes from employer career pages and hiring platforms.
Contact us with a source URL to request correction or removal.


3. PURPOSES AND LEGAL GROUNDS

We use this information to create and secure accounts, provide search,
watchlists, Narrowed and application tracking, deliver account emails and
requested alerts, manage subscriptions, answer support requests, prevent
abuse, maintain reliable service, and meet legal obligations.

Swiss data protection law applies to our processing. Where the EU or UK
GDPR applies, we rely on performance of the service contract for requested
features and billing; legitimate interests for security, diagnostics and
service improvement; legal obligations where relevant; and consent where
required, including optional communications. You can withdraw consent
without affecting processing that lawfully occurred before withdrawal.

We do not sell personal data or use it to create advertising profiles.


4. SEARCH, NARROWED AND SHARING

TypeSafe AI provides the model used to interpret natural-language searches
and to check job descriptions against Narrowed criteria. For search we
send the query text and language. For Narrowed we send normalized criteria
and job identifiers, titles, company names and description text. We do not
include your account email, password or application-tracking notes in
these model requests. Information you put into the query or criteria is
nevertheless included.

Narrowed evaluates postings, not applicants. It helps you choose which
jobs to view; it does not make hiring decisions. Results can be incomplete
or mistaken. Review the original posting and make your own decisions.

TypeSafe's published policy says it does not train or fine-tune models on
customer inputs. It does not promise a fixed deletion period for our
standard API use; we do not promise zero data retention.

Watchlists you publish are visible to others. Unlisted sharing makes the
shared information accessible to anyone with the link. Check the sharing
setting before including personal information. Applying through an
employer's website is subject to that employer's own privacy practices.


