6. SECURITY

We use HTTPS for the website, password hashing for email/password accounts,
restricted access to production systems, and encrypted recovery backups.
These measures reduce risk; they do not guarantee absolute security or
mean that every internal processing step is end-to-end encrypted.


7. COOKIES AND BROWSER STORAGE

We use authentication/session cookies and browser storage for functions
such as sign-in and saved preferences. Some persist beyond a browser
session. We do not use advertising cookies. Vercel Web Analytics uses
cookie-free aggregate measurements; operational request logs are separate
and can contain technical identifiers. Paddle's checkout uses its own
technologies and notices for payment processing and fraud prevention.


8. YOUR RIGHTS

Under the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection and, where applicable, the
EU or UK GDPR, you can request information/access, correction, deletion
and, where the relevant conditions apply, a portable copy, restriction of
processing, or object to processing. You may withdraw consent at any time.
Some data must be retained for legal obligations or legitimate claims.

Contact business@colophon-group.org. We may verify your identity before
acting and will respond within the applicable legal deadline, normally
one month. You can contact the Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information
Commissioner (https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/) or the competent authority where
you live. You can also delete your account in account settings.


9. RETENTION AND DELETION

Account and user-created records are generally kept while your account
is active or the feature needs them. Account deletion removes the account
and linked application records from the active database. Narrowed matching
decisions are scheduled for cleanup after 30 days from evaluation; saved
criteria and related configuration remain until changed or deleted.

Recovery backups rotate through daily, weekly and monthly recovery points,
including twelve monthly snapshots. Deleted data can therefore remain in
backups for approximately a year, and longer if a backup/rotation failure
requires recovery work. Backups are restricted to recovery purposes;
account deletion does not individually rewrite historical snapshots.

Provider retention is separate. Resend publishes standard email/log
retention of 30 days with additional backup and account-termination windows.
TypeSafe retains data as needed for the purposes described in its policy;
we have not promised a fixed API retention period. Paddle retains purchase
records under its own legal and accounting obligations. Security, support
or dispute records may be retained as needed for those purposes or law.
Contact us if you need a deletion request coordinated with a provider.


